#
# The refused/decided membership pair again, aimed at the STRUCTURED reporter rather than the console
# one, over a CloudFormation-shaped template.
#
# A new file rather than a widened `membership_lead_sentence.guard`, because that fixture's cell
# asserts `membership_lines.len() == 3` and adding or reshaping a rule there would move a count another
# test depends on. Two fixtures with one rule pair each is cheaper than one fixture with two tests
# reading different slices of it.
#
# `Resources` is load-bearing. Without it `CfnAware` hands the file to `generic_summary`, whose sentence
# is built by `membership_verdict` -- a different site with its own coverage. The CloudFormation shape is
# what routes the report through `common::report_from_events` and so through the `ClauseCheck::InComparison`
# arm in `eval_context.rs`, which is the site this fixture exists to reach.
#
# `k_refused` names a pattern that compiles and then exhausts fancy-regex's backtracking budget on the
# eighteen-character key, so nothing was compared. `k_decided` names both keys literally, so the
# comparison genuinely answered. One report, both arms of the conditional.
#
rule k_refused {
    Resources.*.Properties.Cfg[ keys not in [/(?!x)((a+)+)b/] ] !empty
}

rule k_decided {
    Resources.*.Properties.Cfg[ keys not in ["aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "other"] ] !empty
}
